\paragraph{RE: oracle routing.}
Oracle routing achieves 0.802 accuracy versus 0.504 single-pass on FewRel 80-relation RE (+29.8\,pp; Table~\ref{tab:batch_composition}); type separation thus recovers performance absent merge amplification. Confusability-aware grouping yields only +1.4\,pp over random ($p \approx 0.19$, n.s.); all practical routing strategies fall below the single-pass baseline because constrained decoding forces confident predictions in every sub-schema (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_routing}).

\paragraph{Future directions.}
Three avenues may address these bottlenecks: (1)~coarse-to-fine pipelines that screen with the full schema then refine with targeted sub-schemas; (2)~retrieval-based routing using document retrieval rather than LLM confidence for sub-schema assignment; (3)~calibrated generation \citep{jagannatha2020calibrating} to recover confidence signals eliminated by constrained decoding.

